# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context filter for BOTH published images (agent and verifier).
#
# Rule 0 of this benchmark: the published images carry the public task material
# only. One private contestant depends on proprietary software and infrastructure
# that cannot be redistributed, so its adapter lives under private/ and is excluded here.
# private/ is not part of the public repository at all; this rule is what keeps
# it out of an image in an operator's checkout, where it does exist.
# See policy.PUBLIC_IMAGE_FORBIDDEN (src/dmaic_harbor/policy.py, host-side only).
#
# tests/test_public_image_hygiene.py enforces every rule below.
# =============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- THE POLICY
private
private/
private/**
**/private
**/private/**

# Belt and braces: anything named after an excluded stack, anywhere. The vendor-specific
# patterns are NOT written here -- a public file listing the names we exclude re-discloses
# exactly what the exclusion is for. An operator appends their own to a local copy; the
# structural rule above is what ships.
**/*operator_agent*
**/*operator_adapter*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- repo noise
.git
.git/**
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.github/**
**/.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- run output
runs
runs/**
jobs
jobs/**
trials
trials/**
**/*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- caches / venvs
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.pytest_cache/**
.ruff_cache
.ruff_cache/**
.mypy_cache
.mypy_cache/**
.coverage
htmlcov
htmlcov/**
.venv
.venv/**
venv
venv/**
build
build/**
dist
dist/**
*.egg-info
*.egg-info/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- credentials
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa*
**/credentials
**/credentials.*
**/secrets
**/secrets.*
**/.netrc
**/.npmrc
**/.docker/config.json
**/settings.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- host-only material
# These are operator/orchestrator files. They are also the only public files
# permitted to name the excluded stack (to document why it is excluded), so
# keeping them out of every image is what makes that permission safe. The hygiene
# test asserts exactly this pairing.
tests
tests/**
docs
docs/**
job.example.yaml
README.md
reference
reference/**
.gitignore
.dockerignore
